All six round-1 candidates scored 0, on dev and in training. Ruled out as the only problem: an action frame in set A or set B, an obs reorientation combined with an A or B layout, and a scale deviation fixed by LayerNorm with set A. Because nothing scored, there is no hedge to split yet. Following step 5 of the program, this round tries things not yet tested:
- type-minor action indexing (K innermost) with sets A and B;
- the stacked hedge combination that escaped zero in world 3 (obs symmetries, LayerNorm, global context in each residual block, a dilated block), with set A and with set B;
- a fully learned dense mask embedding and dense placement head, which covers any action permutation or an n_place that differs from K·Y·X;
- the separate-critic fallback (gamma 0.99, ent 0.01) on the combined net.

If one of these scores, round 3 splits it. If all score 0, the deviation is probably not a frame mismatch, and dynamics or reward become the suspects.
